Paart turns the WireGuard instances a firewall already runs into managed
user access: named identities, one key per device, immediate revocation
and an audit journal.

Administrators think in people and access rather than configuration
files. Private keys are generated on the devices and never travel, so the
firewall never holds one. The plugin attaches to instances the
administrator declares and touches nothing else: no instance it was not
given, no address outside the declared ranges, and never a peer removed
without an explicit intention.

Devices enrol by scanning a QR code, either from the Apple application or
from the built-in web portal for other platforms. Nothing depends on a
publisher's server, at any point.

WWW: https://paart.app
